 "drivingQuestion": "Why does the mishna not list exploitation of a peruta?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "Rav Kahana infers no exploitation for perutot (disputed by Levi in the next unit).",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "bava_metzia.55a.11",
   "daf": "55a",
   "sentenceId": 10,
   "he": "חָמֵשׁ פְּרוּטוֹת הֵן כּוּ׳. וְלִיתְנֵי נָמֵי הָאוֹנָאָה פְּרוּטָה? אָמַר רַב כָּהֲנָא: זֹאת אוֹמֶרֶת, אֵין אוֹנָאָה לִפְרוּטוֹת.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «There are five» halakhic situations involving «perutot.» The Gemara asks: «And let» the tanna «also teach» that «the» measure of «exploitation» is «one peruta. Rav Kahana said: That is to say» that «there is no exploitation concerning perutot.» Any disparity between value and price that is less than the value of the smallest silver coin, an issar, which is worth eight perutot, is not considered exploitation."
  }
 ],
